    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50470" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventrĭōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		venter, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>having a large belly</i>, <i>big -
				bellied</i>, <i>pot - bellied</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 2, 3, 20</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Merc. 3, 4, 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ps. 4,
				7, 120</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Rud. 2, 2, 11</span></i>.—In the
			collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventrŭōsus</span></b> , <i>bellying out</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventruosa ac patula dolia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 21, 27, § 134</span></i>
			; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventrōsus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Cassiod. in Psa.
				72</span></i>.</div>
